title: Amit_Day1
tags: 
position: -7,-175
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite KohliwadaGround>>

// Scene Setup - Day 1 at Koliwada Ground
After finishing practice with Ramu, Raju visits Koliwada Ground where his friend Amit has been waiting, hoping to organize a proper cricket match.

The dusty expanse of Koliwada Ground stretches before Raju. Amit sits on a boundary stone with obvious frustration, his cricket bat beside him. His eyes scan the empty ground with disappointed expression, stranded between boredom and persistent hope.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amit" "Disappointed">>
Amit: Raju yaar, I'm so frustrated! I've been waiting here for two hours.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amit" "Irritated">>
Amit: I was hoping to organize a decent cricket match, but we don't have enough proper equipment for everyone who wants to play.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: That's really annoying, Amit! What exactly are we missing?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Maybe there's a way to solve this problem if we think creatively about it.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amit" "Worried">>
Amit: We need at least two more cricket balls for a proper match.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amit" "Disappointed">>
Amit: Plus some decent wickets that won't fall over every time someone bowls fast.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amit" "Sad">>
Amit: The boys are getting impatient and some have already left to find other games.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: This is a real problem, but I'm sure cricket equipment must be available somewhere in our neighborhood.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: We just need to be systematic about finding it instead of giving up.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amit" "Smiling">>
Amit: You're always good at solving problems, Raju!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amit" "Tired">>
Amit: But I've already asked all the usual people and checked the obvious places.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amit" "Skeptical">>
Amit: This might require more creative thinking than I can manage right now.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Confident">>
Raju: Then let's approach this systematically.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Cricket equipment doesn't just disappear - it gets stored, forgotten, or overlooked.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: If we search carefully and think about all the possible locations, we should find what we need.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amit" "Quizzical">>
Amit: True! Sometimes balls roll into drains or get stuck in unusual places.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amit" "Smiling">>
Amit: And people forget they put wickets away after previous matches. We might find equipment in places no one thinks to look.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Exactly! Or maybe someone has extra equipment at home but doesn't realize we need it.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Confident">>
Raju: We should check with more people and explore areas around the ground more thoroughly.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
As Raju prepares to leave with a clear mission, he carries determination to find practical solutions. The challenge has transformed from simple disappointment into an opportunity to demonstrate that obstacles can be overcome through systematic effort.

<<set $Amit_Day = 2>>
<<EndEvent true>>
===

title: Amit_Day2
tags: 
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite KohliwadaGround>>

// Scene Setup - Day 2 returning with new ideas
Despite the unsuccessful initial search, Raju returns to meet Amit at Koliwada Ground, bringing new ideas about where they might find needed supplies.

The familiar setting welcomes Raju with renewed optimism. His reflection has generated several promising strategies for locating cricket supplies. Amit's presence reflects both continued hope and mounting frustration as another day threatens to pass.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amit" "Smiling">>
Amit: Back again, yaar? I was hoping you might have some new ideas about finding cricket equipment.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amit" "Sad">>
Amit: The search didn't turn up much, but maybe we missed some obvious possibilities.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Confident">>
Raju: Actually, I spent some time thinking about this problem.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I have several new strategies we could try. Sometimes the best solutions come from approaching familiar problems with fresh perspectives.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amit" "Excited">>
Amit: That's exactly what we need - fresh thinking!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amit" "Determined">>
Amit: I was getting so focused on the usual places that I probably missed creative alternatives. What new approaches did you come up with?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: Well, I was thinking about all the different ways cricket equipment might end up in unexpected places.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: And all the people who might have supplies they're not currently using.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: For example, maybe some families stored cricket gear after their children outgrew it.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Confident">>
Raju: Or equipment got left behind after tournaments and no one claimed it. We should expand our search beyond just active players.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amit" "Astonished">>
Amit: That's brilliant thinking! I was only asking current cricket players.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amit" "Excited">>
Amit: But you're right - lots of people might have unused equipment sitting around.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amit" "Determined">>
Amit: Former players, families with older children, even shops that might have damaged items they can't sell.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Exactly! And we should also consider making temporary equipment if we can't find enough ready-made supplies.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Mischievous">>
Raju: Sometimes creative improvisation works better than waiting for perfect conditions.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amit" "Proud">>
Amit: You're absolutely right about improvisation.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amit" "Smiling">>
Amit: Our parents' generation played cricket with makeshift equipment all the time. We shouldn't let perfect be the enemy of good.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amit" "Serious">>
Amit: How should we organize this search to maximize our chances of success?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amit" "Determined">>
Amit: What's the best strategy for covering all these different possibilities?

<<HideAllCharacters>>
As their planning session concludes with expanded strategies and renewed optimism, both boys understand that the disappointment has evolved into more sophisticated understanding of resource management and creative problem-solving.

<<set $Amit_Day = 3>>
<<EndEvent true>>
===

